From 3607dd93b49b04b0b2323201d621ebbe49198cde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Sotraidis <56282582+chrissotraidis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 08:08:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 73/74] frontend: reuse one render packet instead of zeroing a
 draw snapshot per event

RenderPacket carries RenderDrawPacket, the draw's full matrix, light and XF
snapshot (about 2.5 KB), and emit_new_packets built a fresh packet for every
trace event, so each BP/XF/CP state event zeroed it. That memset was 9 percent
of the GX translation worker in a sample of the iPad simulator's heavy Outset
view. The frontend now reuses one packet and clears its draw section only for a
Draw event and the event after one, so every packet a sink sees still reads as
freshly built. make_render_packet keeps its by-value form on top of the new
in-place fill_render_packet.

Rendered play window in the save's Outset view: 568 -> 542 M host instructions
per retrace; seven captured frames byte-identical.
